tion 5.2, so we need only specify the Setup algorithm and define how an
identity \emph{id} maps to a KEM public

key \textbf{A}\emph{id∥}\textbf{y}\emph{id}. Let \emph{H} :
\emph{\{}0\emph{,} 1\emph{\}∗→}Z\emph{n×m} oracles.

and \emph{G} : \emph{\{}0\emph{,} 1\emph{\}∗→}Z\emph{n q}be hash
functions modelled as random

\begin{quote}
