\textbf{5.4.6} \textbf{Proof of Theorem 5.4}

We proceed in games, with \textbf{Game} 0 being the original aid-ind-cpa
experiment with adversary \emph{A}. We assume without loss of generality
that \emph{A} always makes exactly \emph{Q} = \emph{Q}(\emph{n}) user
secret key queries. We denote these queries by \emph{idj}= (\emph{idj}
1\emph{, . . . , idjℓj}) (for 1 \emph{≤j ≤Q}), and the challenge
identity chosen by \emph{A} as \emph{id∗}= (\emph{id∗}1\emph{, . . . ,
id∗ℓ∗}). By \emph{outi}, we denote the experiment's output in Game
\emph{i}. By definition,

