\emph{controlled.} Now in Game 4, we will set up the public key as
follows:

\begin{quote}
\emph{•} \textbf{A}0 as controlled (as in the earlier games),\\
\emph{•} \textbf{B}\emph{i,u,b} as controlled if \emph{Ki u}= \emph{b}
(and as undirected if \emph{Ki u̸}= \emph{b}).

By Proposition 3.1, this change affects the distribution of the public
key only negligibly. (Note that bases for the controlled
\textbf{B}\emph{i,u,b} are generated, but never used in Game 4.) We
obtain

