In \textbf{Game} 5, we make the following conceptual change regarding
user secret key queries. Namely, upon receiving a user secret key
request for \emph{id} = (\emph{id}1\emph{, . . . , idℓ}), the experiment
immediately aborts (with uniform output) if \emph{Fi}(\emph{idi}) = UN
for all \emph{i}. This change is purely conceptual: since \emph{id} is
not a prefix of the challenge identity \emph{id∗}, there is an \emph{i}
with \emph{idi ∈ID}CO\emph{⊇IDQ i\textbackslash{} ID∗i}. But since
\emph{Fi}(\emph{idi}) = UN for this \emph{i}, there is a partial
identity \emph{idi ∈ID}COwhich \emph{should} map to a controlled matrix
but does not (since actually \emph{Fi}(\emph{idi}) = UN).
\end{quote}

